# scratch space: params files with absolute paths, diagnostic scripts, tool inputs.
# See local/README.md, itself ignored.
#
# MUST keep the leading slash. A bare `local/` matches a directory of that name at
# ANY depth, which silently ignored the whole of `modules/local/`. Existing files
# there stayed tracked, so nothing looked wrong until a NEW local module was added
# and `git add` refused it; the module then went missing from its own commit while
# the workflow that included it was committed fine.
/local/
